-- testdata/fill: the width boundary, which is the only place an off-by-one
-- in the measurement shows up. This file is CANONICAL: `wokfmt` must
-- reproduce it byte for byte.
--
-- type alternatives: the FIRST one stays on the `=` line, because a break
-- before it would put an item lead at the head of the next line.
--
-- 80 columns, so it stays on one line: 80 is the last width that fits.
module M

type Shape = Circle U64 | Square U64 | Rect U64 U64 | Triangle U64 U64 | Dxxxxxx
